 ### 3.1 f_tf_glyph — glyph-field renderer (already on your roster, row 13)                                                      
                                                                                                                                 
 Ellipse/cross/stick per cell, from λ₁, λ₂, θ. The two knobs the audience sees: scale and threshold (draw ellipse only above     
 trace/energy gate). Collapse test: losing λ₂ collapses the ellipse to a line or a circle — the glyph is the second eigenvalue   
 made visible. Diagnostics + a look all in one; the field is both content and renderer input. GPU: closed-form per cell, no      
 loop.                                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                                 
 ### 3.2 f_tf_aniso_blur — coherence-enhancing smoothing (row 12, your strongest candidate)                                      
                                                                                                                                 
 Ellipse-integration kernel: sample-source integrated along edge, width ∝ anisotropy. Collapse test: a vecfield gives one axis,  
 not a kernel shape — a coherence-enhancing blend needs λ₂ (what survives across the edge) and λ₁ (how far along to integrate);  
 collapsing loses the elliptical falloff and with it the painterly "smear along, not across" look. Knobs: length (integration    
 steps), coherence gate (how much of the kernel collapses to isotropic at low coherence). Fallback isotropic where field is flat 
 — per Weickert (https://www.mia.uni-saarland.de/weickert/Papers/book.pdf), diffusivity falls back to scalar when eigenvalues    
 are near-equal, so this is principled, not a bolt-on. GPU: bounded 8–16-tap ellipse; real-time.                                 
                                                                                                                                 
 ### 3.3 f_tf_temporal — tensor-space temporal smoother (row 14, your row 14)                                                    
                                                                                                                                 
 Tensor-space one-pole: T' = T + k(T_new − T'), per component. Collapse test: opposite edges crossing each other average         
 correctly in tensor space (reinforce/dampen per the hub's own argument); a vecfield one-pole gives mush where directions flip   
 sign. Knobs: attack, release — the performable "grain release" gesture. Prereq for stable video; also is the inertia gesture.   
 GPU: one pass, one feedback texture, zero loops, bounded.                                                                       
                                                                                                                                 
